From: Daniele Masato <daniele.masato@pm.me>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: mm: reserve the DTB before scanning reserved-memory

Since commit ef69d2559fe9 ("riscv: Move early dtb mapping into the fixmap
region"), setup_bootmem() calls early_init_fdt_scan_reserved_mem() before
memblock_reserve() of the DTB. Dynamically placed /reserved-memory regions
(size only, no reg) are allocated in that scan, so one can land on the DTB.
Linux keeps the unflattened tree's property values in that blob, so a
driver that clears its region wipes the device tree.

On the NanoKVM Lite U-Boot leaves the DTB at 0x8e712000; a 75 MiB
size-only region was placed at 0x8b300000..0x8fdfffff over it, and
soph_sys zeroed it at probe. Reserve the DTB first, as before 6.4.
Reserving is not an allocation, so the scan still runs before any.

Fixes: ef69d2559fe9 ("riscv: Move early dtb mapping into the fixmap region")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/arch/riscv/mm/init.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/mm/init.c
@@ -297,13 +297,6 @@
 	dma32_phys_limit = min(4UL * SZ_1G, (unsigned long)PFN_PHYS(max_low_pfn));
 
 	reserve_initrd_mem();
-
-	/*
-	 * No allocation should be done before reserving the memory as defined
-	 * in the device tree, otherwise the allocation could end up in a
-	 * reserved region.
-	 */
-	early_init_fdt_scan_reserved_mem();
 
 	/*
 	 * If DTB is built in, no need to reserve its memblock.
@@ -314,6 +307,13 @@
 	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_BUILTIN_DTB))
 		memblock_reserve(dtb_early_pa, fdt_totalsize(dtb_early_va));
 
+	/*
+	 * No allocation should be done before reserving the memory as defined
+	 * in the device tree, otherwise the allocation could end up in a
+	 * reserved region.
+	 */
+	early_init_fdt_scan_reserved_mem();
+
 	dma_contiguous_reserve(dma32_phys_limit);
 	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_64BIT))
 		hugetlb_cma_reserve(PUD_SHIFT - PAGE_SHIFT);
